flowchart TB
  accTitle: What a run by hand may do
  accDescr: A run by hand of issue-assistant.yml, from the Actions tab, gh workflow run or the REST API, names an issue, a task, an optional instruction and the override. The job event asks GitHub for the role of the person who started the run, or who ran it again. Without write access, the run fails before anything is written and before the AI. With override, only the roles admin and maintain may go on, and the summary of the run records the override; the AI then answers again, even where its task already has its comment. Without override, a triage or follow-up that already has its comment stops without the AI, and every other run goes on to the AI, which reads the instruction after its task. The job apply checks the role again and the answer as always, and the assistant's bot posts the comment.
  start(["a run by hand: issue,<br>task, instruction,<br>override"]) --> role{"role of the person<br>who started it?"}
  role -- "read, triage or none" --> refused["the run fails:<br>nothing written,<br>no AI"]
  role -- "write, maintain<br>or admin" --> override{"override?"}
  override -- "yes, but only write" --> refused
  override -- "yes, admin<br>or maintain" --> logged["the summary records<br>the override"]
  override -- "no" --> answered{"its triage or follow-up<br>already answered?"}
  answered -- "yes" --> once["no AI run: the<br>assistant answers once"]
  answered -- "no" --> ai["`**the AI** answers,<br>with the instruction<br>after its task`"]
  logged --> ai
  ai --> apply["apply checks the role<br>again and the answer;<br>the bot posts it"]
  classDef trigger fill:#d4a72c33,stroke:#bf8700,stroke-width:2px
  classDef question fill:#d4a72c33,stroke:#bf8700,stroke-width:2px
  classDef ai fill:#8250df33,stroke:#8250df,stroke-width:2px
  classDef job fill:#8c959f1f,stroke:#8c959f,stroke-width:2px
  class start trigger
  class role,override,answered question
  class ai ai
  class refused,logged,once,apply job
